      "id": "CONFIG_EMPTY",
      "conclusion": "No production blocker found",
      "locations": [
        "crates/cc-index/src/indexer_phases/snapshot.rs:29",
        "crates/cc-index/src/indexer_phases/snapshot.rs:50",
        "crates/cc-index/src/indexer_phases/config_link.rs:43",
        "crates/cc-index/src/config_linker.rs:208"
      ],
      "reason": "The original unconditional signature-then-config-scan and typed-project-config filtering remain before the new guard. The moved collectors only clone immutable write-unit symbol/path values. With zero filtered tokens, resolve_config_links iterates no tokens and produces no links; its snapshot adapter returned empty at line 83 before any per-config filesystem read at line 98. Thus this branch removes unused in-memory preparation, not input validation, filesystem error handling or DB work. Nonempty tokens still receive the original builder and identical values.",
      "preserved": [
        "empty-token cache serialization",
        "config signature and algorithm metadata",
        "last_indexed_at generation and writes",
        "typed module/config resolution",
        "full snapshot replacement and stale config removal",
        "common staging/temp-db/DirectWriter adapters",
        "incremental config path"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "INTERFACE_PREREQUISITES",
      "conclusion": "No production blocker found under the existing production schema",
      "locations": [
        "crates/cc-index/src/dispatch_synthesis/interface_dispatch.rs:46",
        "crates/cc-db/src/index_db_graph.rs:440",
        "crates/cc-db/src/index_db_graph.rs:479",
        "crates/cc-db/src/index_db_edges.rs:258",
        "crates/cc-db/src/sql/index_v1.sql:155"
      ],
      "reason": "CALL rows and prior CALL deltas remain first. The no-call return still precedes all symbol reads. All symbol_dispatch_rows are typed-decoded into a Result<Vec<_>> before the new interface test. The schema declares symbols.symbol_uid TEXT UNIQUE, so selecting nonempty interface/trait UIDs directly from decoded rows is equivalent to selecting from the old uid map. With an interface, implements UID pairs are fully typed-decoded before the new empty-pairs return. An empty implements map in the old implementation was equivalent to empty pairs because each pair unconditionally inserts. Only lookup allocations move; no SQL getter is elided beyond the old no-call/no-interface boundaries.",
      "error_order": "CALL -> symbols -> implements preserved; malformed rows and query errors still propagate at the old read boundaries",
      "schema_boundary": "No claim for arbitrary manually weakened/replaced tables without the existing UNIQUE constraint."
    },
    {
      "id": "CLEANUP_AND_POSITIVE_PATH",
      "conclusion": "Preserved",
      "reason": "Enabled passes set delete_call_kinds=['interface_dispatch'] before prerequisite returns; disabled passes still return default with no cleanup/read. Original prior CALL replacement and overlay, map row insertion order, same-name container candidate vectors, fanout cap, self-reference exclusion, edge fields/UIDs and final edge_id deduplication are unchanged. PassContext explicitly covers CALL overlays only and earlier passes currently do not emit implements; this contract is unchanged. Moving pure maps does not upgrade the existing separate read queries into a transaction-wide snapshot."
    },
    {
      "id": "COST_SCOPE",
      "conclusion": "Only a conditional avoided-allocation claim is supported statically",
      "reason": "Empty heuristic tokens avoid cloning all symbol/path catalogs and constructing their lookup indexes; no interface/implements consumer avoids otherwise unused symbol/container maps. Full source/config scanning and typed symbol/implements SQL reads required by original guards remain. No measured elapsed time/RSS gain, no 100k causal attribution, no new capacity or quality acceptance is demonstrated by this PR's local test logs."
    }
  ],
